  "id": "ghina_rifi_iraqi",
  "name": "Ghināʾ rīfī (southern Iraqi rural song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Rural song of southern Iraq around Nasiriyah, Amarah and the Mesopotamian marshes, sung in the southern dialect and centred on the abudhiya, a four-line poem whose first three lines end in a punning homonym and whose last ends in -iyya, delivered in a long free-rhythm melismatic style before a measured song. Singers such as Hudhairi Abu Aziz and Dakhil Hassan brought it to Iraqi Radio in the mid-20th century.",
  "recipe": "classic early-1940s ghināʾ rīfī, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. neutral third half flat, many notes per syllable, solo unaccompanied. am radio booth. Neumann U47, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, Telefunken u73b broadcast comp. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
